.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt PING 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ping
.Nd send ICMP echo requests through the net: service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Op Fl s Ar bytes
.Ar host
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens
.Dq net:icmp/ Ns Ar host
and sends ICMP echo requests through the native
.Dq net:
service. The target must be a dotted-quad IPv4 address.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar count
Send at most
.Ar count
requests, from 1 to 1000. The default is 4.
.It Fl w Ar seconds
Bound the whole run to
.Ar seconds
seconds, from 1 to 60. The default is 5. Each request uses the remaining budget as its reply
deadline.
.It Fl s Ar bytes
Send
.Ar bytes
payload bytes in each request, from 0 to 1400. The default is 32.
.El
.Pp
Every request carries one echo identifier and an increasing sequence number. For each reply
.Nm
prints the sequence number and the round-trip time measured by the server, followed by a summary
with the transmitted and received counts, the loss percentage and the minimum, average and maximum
round-trip time. A timeout is reported as
.Dq timeout
and counted as loss.
.Pp
The tool exits 0 only when every requested echo was sent and answered. A timeout, a refused
request, a malformed address or an invalid option exits non-zero.
.Pp
Only the
.Dq net:
scheme API is used. No raw socket is opened and no interface address is read.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr netstat 1 ,
.Xr route 1 ,
.Xr netd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
